  "title": "Amina of Zazzau",
  "summary": "Queen Amina is traditionally said to have ruled the Hausa city-state of Zazzau, present-day Zaria, for thirty-four years after her brother Karama died around 1576, expanding it south and west and credited with defensive walls. Her dates are approximate (c. 1533–c. 1610), her campaigns are \"reported\", and her main source is a book written shortly after her death.",
